# aux-fixed-self-before: Does `aux f=f+1` above a fixed quantity f read the fixed quantity (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: f=4
# pc: ok
# ruling: pc-ode accepts it. The `f` on the right side is the fixed quantity below it, so the column is 4 at x=1 (language.md, Names and order).
x'=-x
x(0)=1
aux f=f+1
f=2*x+1
@ total=1,dt=0.5
